ivacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-08T00:51:34Z","updated_at":"2026-01-08T01:03:35Z","body":"The image shows the front view in local coordinate mode.\n\n<img width=\"1040\" height=\"476\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2b2d6f20-11d8-4d9c-9fec-1f5ea8b50ac5\" />\n\nThe blue gizmo indicates performing a local Z rotation with the Y axis rotated by 0.2 degrees.\nThe outer circle uses the view plane, meaning it represents a global Z rotation.\n\nThe latter case can actually be resolved by using global coordinate mode. However, this example is presented solely for clarity. Since it's unpredictable when such subtle rotational differences might occur, I'm arguing that a default margin should be present.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3721449084/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3721460722","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114674#issuecomment-3721460722","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114674","id":3721460722,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7d0Pvy","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/